Dissemination
Dissemination indicators measure the action of sharing statistical information widely. Data dissemination
standards have become an important area for national statistical offices as a way to communicate data
effectively. Dissemination standards have helped countries to provide economic and financial data to the
public and enhance the availability of timely and comprehensive statistics.
Two widely used indicators of dissemination are the International Monetary Fund’s (IMF) data dissemination
standards (GDDS/SDDS/SDDS plus) and Open Data Watch’s Open Data Inventory (ODIN) index. The Special Data


